/-!
# Derivatives of ideals and maximal contact (Kollár, *Resolution*, §3.d, 3.73–3.96)

Let `X` be a smooth scheme over a field `k`. The *first derivative* `D(I)` of an ideal sheaf
`I ⊆ 𝒪_X` is the ideal sheaf generated by the `δ(f)`, `δ` a local `k`-derivation of `𝒪_X` and
`f` a local section of `I`; iterating gives `D^r(I)`, and for `m = maxord I ≥ 1` the *maximal
contact ideal* is `MC(I) = D^{m-1}(I)` (Kollár 3.73, 3.79). This file states these notions,
their logarithmic versions along a smooth hypersurface (3.87), the partial derivatives with
respect to local coordinates (3.73, 3.87.2), `D`-balanced and MC-invariant ideals (3.83, 3.53),
the marked derivatives `D^r(I, m) = (D^r I, m - r)` (3.73.3), the transforms `T_i(K, a)` of
Cor. 3.77, hypersurfaces of maximal contact (3.78), étale equivalence of blow-up sequences and of
hypersurfaces (3.96, §3.10), formal equivalence of hypersurfaces of maximal contact (3.91), the
derivative ideals of a ring (3.74(5), 3.93) and automorphisms of `K[[x_1, …, x_n]]` of the form
`1 + B` (3.93).

## Main definitions

* `MMP.Resolution.derivativeIdealOfRing`, `MMP.Resolution.higherDerivativeIdealOfRing`:
  `D_{R/A₀}(J)` and `D^r_{R/A₀}(J)` for an ideal `J` of an `A₀`-algebra `R`.
* `MMP.Resolution.derivativeIdeal`, `MMP.Resolution.higherDerivativeIdeal`,
  `MMP.Resolution.maximalContactIdeal`: `D(I)`, `D^r(I)`, `MC(I)`.
* `MMP.Resolution.IsLocalCoordinatesOn`, `MMP.Resolution.IsLocalCoordinatesAt`: local
  coordinates in the sense of Kollár Def. 3.73 (`dx_1, …, dx_n` a basis of `Ω_{U/k}`).
* `MMP.Resolution.partialDerivative`: `∂h/∂x_i`.
* `MMP.Resolution.IsDBalanced`, `MMP.Resolution.IsMCInvariant`.
* `MMP.Resolution.MarkedIdeal.derivative`, `MMP.Resolution.MarkedIdeal.logDerivative`.
* `MMP.Resolution.ClosedBlowupSequence.derivedTransform`,
  `MMP.Resolution.ClosedBlowupSequence.derivedTransformJ`: `T_r(K, a)` and the `J_r` of 3.77.
* `MMP.Resolution.logDerivations`, `MMP.Resolution.logDerivativeIdeal`,
  `MMP.Resolution.higherLogDerivativeIdeal`: `Der_X(-log S)`, `D(-log S)`, `D^r(-log S)`.
* `MMP.Resolution.partialDerivativeIdeal`: `∂^i_{x_j} J`.
* `MMP.Resolution.IsHypersurfaceOfMaximalContact`.
* `MMP.Resolution.IsEtaleChartPair`, `MMP.Resolution.ClosedBlowupSequence.AreEtaleEquivalent`,
  `MMP.Resolution.AreEtaleEquivalentHypersurfaces`.
* `MMP.Resolution.completedIdeal`, `MMP.Resolution.AreFormallyEquivalent`.
* `MMP.Resolution.IsAutomorphismOfFormOnePlus`.

## Implementation notes

The sheaf of derivations `Der_X` (Kollár Def. 3.73) is the library's: over an open `V`, a
`k`-derivation of `𝒪_V` is `Stacks.Curves.SheafDerivationOf (V.ι ≫ s_X)`, and on an affine open
`W` it is the same as a `k`-derivation `Γ(X, W) → Γ(X, W)` of the ring of sections (Mathlib's
`Derivation`), `Γ(X, W)` being a `k`-algebra by `MMP.Mori.sectionAlgebra`. Since `𝒪_X`-ideal
sheaves are determined on affine opens and every local section is locally a section over an
affine open, the ideal sheaf generated by the `δ(f)` (`V` open, `δ ∈ Der_X(V)`, `f ∈ I(V)`) is the
smallest quasi-coherent ideal sheaf `J` with `δ(f) ∈ J(W)` for every affine open `W`, every
`k`-derivation `δ` of `Γ(X, W)` and every `f ∈ I(W)`; this is how `derivativeIdeal` is defined.
That its sections over an affine open are the ideal generated by these `δ(f)`
(`derivativeIdeal_ideal`), and that it is the ideal sheaf generated by the values of the sheaf
derivations over all opens (`derivativeIdeal_eq_sInf_sheafDerivation`), are theorems. The
logarithmic and the partial derivative ideals are defined in the same way, as the smallest ideal
sheaf containing the affine-local values.

Likewise "`dx_1, …, dx_n` is a basis of the `𝒪_U`-module `Ω_{U/k}`" is read on affine opens
`W ⊆ U`, where `Ω_{U/k}(W) = Ω_{Γ(X, W)/k}` (Mathlib's `KaehlerDifferential`). The partial
derivative `∂h/∂x_i` is defined on every affine open `W ⊆ U`, as the `i`-th coordinate of `dh`
in the basis `(dx_j)`; that these glue to a section over `U` is a theorem
(`existsUnique_partialDerivative_glue`). The coordinates of Kollár Def. 3.73 are distinct from
those of (3.60.2) (`MMP.Resolution.IsLocalCoordinates`, étale coordinates), though they agree on
a smooth scheme.

The transforms `T_i(K, a)` of Cor. 3.77 are fractional ideal sheaves. Along the recursion only
the integral ones are used: `T_{i+1}` is `𝒪(aF_{i+1})·π_i^*T_i` when `T_i ⊆ 𝒪_{X_i}`, and `0`
otherwise. So `T_i` is recorded as an `Option`: `some J` when `T_i = J` is an ideal sheaf and
`none` when it is a fractional ideal sheaf not contained in `𝒪_{X_i}` (its value is then not
used). `𝒪(aF)·π^*T ⊆ 𝒪` exactly when `π^*T ⊆ 𝒪(-aF) = I_F^a`, and it is then the ideal quotient
`(π^*T : I_F^a)`.

The maximal order `m = maxord I` is an element of `ℕ∞`; it is read in `ℕ` by `ENat.toNat` (an
infinite order, outside the source's domain, is read as `0`). Hypotheses of the source that only
restrict the domain are dropped: smoothness of `X` and of the hypersurfaces `S`, the
non-vanishing of `I` on the components of `X`, `maxord I ≥ 1`, `0 ≤ r ≤ m` (with truncated
subtraction), separatedness of `X`, the condition that the blow-up sequences in 3.96 be of
order `m` and that the hypersurfaces in 3.91 and §3.10 be of maximal contact, and
`B ⊆ 𝔪` in 3.93. A hypersurface of maximal contact is asked to be a smooth hypersurface, which
is part of the notion.

## References

* [J. Kollár, *Lectures on resolution of singularities*, 3.53, 3.73–3.96]
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace IsLocalRing Limits

attribute [-instance] AlgebraicGeometry.IsVariety.toIsIntegral

universe u

namespace MMP.Resolution

/-! ### Derivative ideals of a ring -/

section Ring

variable (A₀ : Type*) {R : Type*} [CommRing A₀] [CommRing R] [Algebra A₀ R]

/-- The *first derivative* `D_{R/A₀}(J)` of an ideal `J` of an `A₀`-algebra `R` (Kollár 3.74(5),
3.93): the ideal generated by all `δ(f)`, `δ ∈ Der_{A₀}(R)` and `f ∈ J`. -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_derivative_ideal_complete_local_ring"]
def derivativeIdealOfRing (J : Ideal R) : Ideal R :=
  Ideal.span {g | ∃ δ : Derivation A₀ R R, ∃ f ∈ J, δ f = g}

/-- The *higher derivatives* `D^r_{R/A₀}(J)`: `D^0_{R/A₀}(J) = J` and
`D^{r+1}_{R/A₀}(J) = D_{R/A₀}(D^r_{R/A₀}(J))` (Kollár 3.74(5), 3.93). -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_derivative_ideal_complete_local_ring"]
def higherDerivativeIdealOfRing (J : Ideal R) (r : ℕ) : Ideal R :=
  (derivativeIdealOfRing A₀)^[r] J

/-- The zeroth higher derivative of `J` is `J` itself. -/
@[simp, mmp "def_kr3d_derivative_ideal_complete_local_ring"]
theorem higherDerivativeIdealOfRing_zero (J : Ideal R) :
    higherDerivativeIdealOfRing A₀ J 0 = J := rfl

/-- `D^{r+1}_{R/A₀}(J) = D_{R/A₀}(D^r_{R/A₀}(J))`. -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_derivative_ideal_complete_local_ring"]
theorem higherDerivativeIdealOfRing_succ (J : Ideal R) (r : ℕ) :
    higherDerivativeIdealOfRing A₀ J (r + 1) =
      derivativeIdealOfRing A₀ (higherDerivativeIdealOfRing A₀ J r) :=
  Function.iterate_succ_apply' _ _ _

end Ring

section RingLocalization

open KaehlerDifferential

variable {k R A : Type*} [CommRing k] [CommRing R] [CommRing A] [Algebra k R] [Algebra k A]
  [Algebra R A] [IsScalarTower k R A] (M : Submonoid R) [IsLocalization M A]

include M

/-- A derivation of `R` extends to a derivation of a localization of `R`. -/
theorem exists_derivation_extend_of_isLocalization (δ : Derivation k R R) :
    ∃ δ' : Derivation k A A, ∀ r, δ' (algebraMap R A r) = algebraMap R A (δ r) := by
  have : Algebra.FormallyEtale R A := Algebra.FormallyEtale.of_isLocalization M
  have hb := isBaseChange_of_formallyEtale k R A
  let g : Ω[R⁄k] →ₗ[R] A := (Algebra.linearMap R A) ∘ₗ δ.liftKaehlerDifferential
  refine ⟨(hb.lift g).compDer (D k A), fun r => ?_⟩
  have h1 : D k A (algebraMap R A r) = map k k R A (D k R r) := by simp
  show hb.lift g (D k A (algebraMap R A r)) = _
  rw [h1, hb.lift_eq]
  simp [g]

/-- A derivation of a localization of a finitely presented algebra `R`, multiplied by a suitable
denominator, comes from a derivation of `R`. -/
theorem exists_derivation_mul_of_isLocalization [Algebra.FinitePresentation k R]
    (δ' : Derivation k A A) :
    ∃ s ∈ M, ∃ δ'' : Derivation k R R,
      ∀ r, algebraMap R A s * δ' (algebraMap R A r) = algebraMap R A (δ'' r) := by
  let d' : Derivation k R A := δ'.compAlgebraMap R
  obtain ⟨h, s, hs⟩ := Module.FinitePresentation.exists_lift_of_isLocalizedModule
    M (Algebra.linearMap R A) d'.liftKaehlerDifferential
  refine ⟨s, s.2, h.compDer (D k R), fun r => ?_⟩
  have := LinearMap.congr_fun hs (D k R r)
  simp only [LinearMap.coe_comp, Function.comp_apply, Algebra.linearMap_apply, LinearMap.smul_apply,
    Derivation.liftKaehlerDifferential_apply] at this
  show _ = algebraMap R A (h (D k R r))
  rw [this, Submonoid.smul_def, Algebra.smul_def, Derivation.liftKaehlerDifferential_comp_D]
  rfl

/-- Forming the first derivative ideal commutes with localization, for a finitely presented
algebra. -/
theorem derivativeIdealOfRing_map_localization [Algebra.FinitePresentation k R] (J : Ideal R) :
    (derivativeIdealOfRing k J).map (algebraMap R A) =
      derivativeIdealOfRing k (J.map (algebraMap R A)) := by
  apply le_antisymm
  · rw [derivativeIdealOfRing, Ideal.map_span, Ideal.span_le]
    rintro _ ⟨_, ⟨δ, g, hg, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨δ', hδ'⟩ := exists_derivation_extend_of_isLocalization (A := A) M δ
    exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨δ', algebraMap R A g, Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hg, hδ' g⟩
  · refine Ideal.span_le.mpr ?_
    rintro _ ⟨δ', x, hx, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨u, hu, δ'', hδ''⟩ := exists_derivation_mul_of_isLocalization M δ'
    obtain ⟨⟨g, s⟩, hgs⟩ := (IsLocalization.mem_map_algebraMap_iff M A).mp hx
    have E4 : x * algebraMap R A s = algebraMap R A g := hgs
    have E3 := congrArg δ' E4
    rw [Derivation.leibniz, smul_eq_mul, smul_eq_mul] at E3
    have E1 := hδ'' g
    have E2 := hδ'' (s : R)
    have key : algebraMap R A (u * (s : R) ^ 2) * δ' x =
        algebraMap R A ((s : R) * δ'' g - g * δ'' s) := by
      simp only [map_mul, map_pow, map_sub]
      linear_combination (algebraMap R A s) * E1 - (algebraMap R A g) * E2 +
        (algebraMap R A s * algebraMap R A u) * E3 -
        (algebraMap R A u * δ' (algebraMap R A s)) * E4
    have hmem : (s : R) * δ'' g - g * δ'' s ∈ derivativeIdealOfRing k J := by
      have h1 : δ'' g ∈ derivativeIdealOfRing k J := Ideal.subset_span ⟨δ'', g, g.2, rfl⟩
      have h2 : δ'' ((s : R) * g) ∈ derivativeIdealOfRing k J :=
        Ideal.subset_span ⟨δ'', _, J.mul_mem_left _ g.2, rfl⟩
      rw [Derivation.leibniz, smul_eq_mul, smul_eq_mul] at h2
      convert sub_mem (Ideal.mul_mem_left _ (2 * (s : R)) h1) h2 using 1
      ring
    have hunit : IsUnit (algebraMap R A (u * (s : R) ^ 2)) :=
      IsLocalization.map_units A (⟨u * (s : R) ^ 2, M.mul_mem hu (M.pow_mem s.2 2)⟩ : M)
    refine (Ideal.unit_mul_mem_iff_mem _ hunit).mp ?_
    rw [key]
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hmem

end RingLocalization

/-! ### Derivative ideals of an ideal sheaf -/

section Sheaf

variable {k : Type u} [Field k] {X : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ Spec (.of k))

/-- The ideal of `Γ(X, W)` generated by the `δ(f)`, `δ` a `k`-derivation of `Γ(X, W)` and
`f ∈ I(W)`, for an affine open `W`. -/
def sectionDerivativeIdeal (I : X.IdealSheafData) (W : X.affineOpens) : Ideal Γ(X, W) :=
  letI := MMP.Mori.sectionAlgebra sX W.1
  derivativeIdealOfRing k (I.ideal W)

/-- The *first derivative* `D(I) ⊆ 𝒪_X` of an ideal sheaf on a scheme over `k` (Kollár Def. 3.73,
(3.73.1)): the ideal sheaf generated by all `δ(f)`, `δ` a local `k`-derivation of `𝒪_X` and `f` a
local section of `I`, i.e. the smallest ideal sheaf whose sections over every affine open `W`
contain `δ(f)` for every `k`-derivation `δ` of `𝒪_X(W)` and every `f ∈ I(W)`. -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_derivative_ideal"]
def derivativeIdeal (I : X.IdealSheafData) : X.IdealSheafData :=
  sInf {J | ∀ W : X.affineOpens, sectionDerivativeIdeal sX I W ≤ J.ideal W}

private theorem sectionAlgebra_res {W' W : X.Opens} (h : W' ≤ W) (c : k) :
    (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op).hom
      (letI := MMP.Mori.sectionAlgebra sX W; algebraMap k Γ(X, W) c) =
      (letI := MMP.Mori.sectionAlgebra sX W'; algebraMap k Γ(X, W') c) := by
  have := Scheme.Hom.appLE_map sX (U := ⊤) (V := W) (V' := W') (by simp) (homOfLE h).op
  exact congrArg (fun t => (((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ t).hom) c) this

/-- On a scheme locally of finite type over `k`, the ideal of `Γ(X, W)` generated by the `δ(f)`,
`f ∈ I(W)`, is compatible with restriction to a basic open `D(f) ⊆ W`. -/
private theorem sectionDerivativeIdeal_map_basicOpen [LocallyOfFiniteType sX]
    (I : X.IdealSheafData) (W : X.affineOpens) (f : Γ(X, W)) :
    (sectionDerivativeIdeal sX I W).map (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le f)).op).hom =
      sectionDerivativeIdeal sX I (X.affineBasicOpen f) := by
  let := MMP.Mori.sectionAlgebra sX W.1
  let := MMP.Mori.sectionAlgebra sX (X.basicOpen f)
  have : Algebra.FinitePresentation k Γ(X, W) :=
    Algebra.FinitePresentation.of_finiteType.mp (MMP.Mori.finiteType_sectionAlgebra sX W.2)
  have : IsScalarTower k Γ(X, W) Γ(X, X.basicOpen f) :=
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq' (by
      ext c
      exact (sectionAlgebra_res sX (X.basicOpen_le f) c).symm)
  have := W.2.isLocalization_basicOpen f
  have h := derivativeIdealOfRing_map_localization (k := k) (A := Γ(X, X.basicOpen f))
    (Submonoid.powers f) (I.ideal W)
  unfold sectionDerivativeIdeal
  rw [← I.map_ideal_basicOpen W f]
  exact h

/-- On a scheme locally of finite type over `k`, the sections of `D(I)` over an affine open `W`
are the ideal generated by the `δ(f)`, `δ ∈ Der_k(𝒪_X(W))` and `f ∈ I(W)`. -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_derivative_ideal"]
theorem derivativeIdeal_ideal [LocallyOfFiniteType sX] (I : X.IdealSheafData)
    (W : X.affineOpens) :
    (derivativeIdeal sX I).ideal W = sectionDerivativeIdeal sX I W := by
  let J₀ : X.IdealSheafData :=
    { ideal := sectionDerivativeIdeal sX I
      map_ideal_basicOpen := sectionDerivativeIdeal_map_basicOpen sX I }
  have hmem : J₀ ∈ {J : X.IdealSheafData | ∀ W : X.affineOpens,
      sectionDerivativeIdeal sX I W ≤ J.ideal W} := fun W => le_rfl
  have : derivativeIdeal sX I = J₀ :=
    le_antisymm (sInf_le hmem) (le_sInf fun J hJ W => hJ W)
  rw [this]

/-- A section `f ∈ 𝒪_X(V)` over an open `V` is a section of the ideal sheaf `I` over `V`: its
restriction to every affine open `W ⊆ V` lies in `I(W)`. -/
def IsSectionOf (I : X.IdealSheafData) {V : X.Opens} (f : Γ(X, V)) : Prop :=
  ∀ (W : X.affineOpens) (h : W.1 ≤ V), (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op).hom f ∈ I.ideal W

/-- The value `δ(f) ∈ 𝒪_X(V)` of a `k`-derivation `δ ∈ Der_X(V)` of `𝒪_V` on `f ∈ 𝒪_X(V)`. -/
def applyDerivation {V : X.Opens} (δ : Stacks.Curves.SheafDerivationOf (V.ι ≫ sX))
    (f : Γ(X, V)) : Γ(X, V) :=
  V.topIso.hom.hom (δ.onSections (U := ⊤) (V.topIso.inv.hom f))

private theorem topIso_baseChange (V : X.Opens) (r : Γ(Spec (.of k), ⊤)) :
    V.topIso.hom.hom ((((V.ι ≫ sX).app ⊤).hom r : Γ(V, ⊤))) =
      (letI := MMP.Mori.sectionAlgebra sX V
       algebraMap k Γ(X, V) ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).hom.hom r)) := by
  have h1 : (((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ Scheme.Hom.appLE sX ⊤ V (by simp)).hom)
      ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).hom.hom r) = (Scheme.Hom.appLE sX ⊤ V (by simp)).hom r := by
    rw [← CommRingCat.comp_apply]
    simp
  refine Eq.trans ?_ h1.symm
  have h2 : (Scheme.Hom.appLE sX ⊤ V (by simp)).hom r =
      (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : V ≤ sX ⁻¹ᵁ ⊤)).op).hom ((sX.app ⊤).hom r) := rfl
  rw [h2]
  show (X.presheaf.map (eqToHom V.ι_image_top.symm).op).hom
    ((X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (x := V.ι ''ᵁ V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ (sX ⁻¹ᵁ ⊤)) (y := sX ⁻¹ᵁ ⊤)
      (by simp)).op).hom ((sX.app ⊤).hom r)) = _
  have := congrArg (fun t => t.hom ((sX.app ⊤).hom r)) (X.presheaf.map_comp
    (homOfLE (x := V.ι ''ᵁ V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ (sX ⁻¹ᵁ ⊤)) (y := sX ⁻¹ᵁ ⊤) (by simp)).op
    (eqToHom V.ι_image_top.symm).op)
  exact this.symm

/-- A derivation of a `k`-algebra from an additive Leibniz map killing `k`. -/
private def derivationOfLeibniz {A : Type*} [CommRing A] [Algebra k A] (d : A →+ A)
    (hmul : ∀ a b, d (a * b) = a * d b + b * d a) (hbase : ∀ c : k, d (algebraMap k A c) = 0) :
    Derivation k A A where
  toFun := d
  map_add' := d.map_add
  map_smul' := fun c a => by
    rw [Algebra.smul_def, hmul, hbase, mul_zero, add_zero, RingHom.id_apply, Algebra.smul_def]
  map_one_eq_zero' := by simpa using hbase 1
  leibniz' := fun a b => by simp [hmul, smul_eq_mul]

/-- Every `k`-derivation of the ring of sections over an affine open `W` is the value on `W` of
a vector field of `𝒪_W`. -/
private theorem exists_sheafDerivation_of_derivation (W : X.affineOpens) :
    letI := MMP.Mori.sectionAlgebra sX W.1
    ∀ δ : Derivation k Γ(X, W) Γ(X, W), ∃ δ' : Stacks.Curves.SheafDerivationOf (W.1.ι ≫ sX),
      ∀ f, applyDerivation sX δ' f = δ f := by
  let := MMP.Mori.sectionAlgebra sX W.1
  intro δ
  have : IsAffine W.1 := W.2
  have key1 : ∀ x, W.1.topIso.hom.hom (W.1.topIso.inv.hom x) = x := fun x => by
    rw [← CommRingCat.comp_apply, Iso.inv_hom_id]; rfl
  have key2 : ∀ x, W.1.topIso.inv.hom (W.1.topIso.hom.hom x) = x := fun x => by
    rw [← CommRingCat.comp_apply, Iso.hom_inv_id]; rfl
  obtain ⟨δ', hδ', -⟩ := Stacks.Curves.existsUnique_sheafDerivationOf_of_isAffine (W.1.ι ≫ sX)
    ({ toFun := fun s => W.1.topIso.inv.hom (δ (W.1.topIso.hom.hom s))
       map_zero' := by rw [map_zero, map_zero, map_zero]
       map_add' := by intros; rw [map_add, map_add, map_add] } : Γ(W.1, ⊤) →+ Γ(W.1, ⊤))
    (fun a b => by
      show W.1.topIso.inv.hom (δ (W.1.topIso.hom.hom (a * b))) =
        a * W.1.topIso.inv.hom (δ (W.1.topIso.hom.hom b)) +
          b * W.1.topIso.inv.hom (δ (W.1.topIso.hom.hom a))
      rw [map_mul, Derivation.leibniz, map_add, smul_eq_mul, smul_eq_mul, map_mul, map_mul, key2,
        key2])
    (fun r => by
      show W.1.topIso.inv.hom
        (δ (W.1.topIso.hom.hom ((((W.1.ι ≫ sX).app ⊤).hom r : Γ(W.1, ⊤))))) = 0
      rw [topIso_baseChange sX W.1 r, Derivation.map_algebraMap, map_zero])
  refine ⟨δ', fun f => ?_⟩
  unfold applyDerivation
  rw [hδ']
  show W.1.topIso.hom.hom (W.1.topIso.inv.hom (δ (W.1.topIso.hom.hom (W.1.topIso.inv.hom f)))) = _
  rw [key1, key1]

private theorem iota_app_restrict {V : X.Opens} {W : X.Opens} (hW : W ≤ V) (f : Γ(X, V)) :
    (V.ι.app W).hom ((X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hW).op).hom f) =
      (V.toScheme.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ W ≤ ⊤)).op).hom
        (V.topIso.inv.hom f) := by
  show (X.presheaf.map _).hom ((X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hW).op).hom f) =
    (X.presheaf.map _).hom ((X.presheaf.map _).hom f)
  rw [← CommRingCat.comp_apply, ← CommRingCat.comp_apply]
  erw [← Functor.map_comp, ← Functor.map_comp]
  rfl

private theorem iota_app_algebraMap (V : X.Opens) (W : X.Opens) (c : k) :
    (V.ι.app W).hom (letI := MMP.Mori.sectionAlgebra sX W; algebraMap k Γ(X, W) c) =
      (V.toScheme.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ W ≤ ⊤)).op).hom
        (((V.ι ≫ sX).app ⊤).hom ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv.hom c)) := by
  have h := Scheme.Hom.appLE_comp_appLE V.ι sX ⊤ W (V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ W) (by simp) le_rfl
  rw [← Scheme.Hom.app_eq_appLE] at h
  exact congrArg (fun t => ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ t).hom c) h

/-- A vector field of `𝒪_V` restricts to a `k`-derivation of the ring of sections over every open
`W ⊆ V` (here with `W` affine). -/
private theorem exists_derivation_of_sheafDerivation {V : X.Opens}
    (δ : Stacks.Curves.SheafDerivationOf (V.ι ≫ sX)) (W : X.affineOpens) (hW : W.1 ≤ V) :
    letI := MMP.Mori.sectionAlgebra sX W.1
    ∃ δW : Derivation k Γ(X, W) Γ(X, W), ∀ f : Γ(X, V),
      (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hW).op).hom (applyDerivation sX δ f) =
        δW ((X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hW).op).hom f) := by
  let := MMP.Mori.sectionAlgebra sX W.1
  have : IsIso (V.ι.app W.1) := Scheme.Hom.isIso_app V.ι W.1 (by simpa using hW)
  let e : Γ(X, W.1) ≃+* Γ(V, V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ W.1) :=
    RingEquiv.ofBijective (V.ι.app W.1).hom (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso _)
  have he : ∀ a, e a = (V.ι.app W.1).hom a := fun _ => rfl
  refine ⟨derivationOfLeibniz
    ({ toFun := fun a => e.symm (δ.onSections (e a))
       map_zero' := by rw [map_zero, Stacks.Curves.SheafDerivationOf.onSections_zero, map_zero]
       map_add' := by
         intros; rw [map_add, Stacks.Curves.SheafDerivationOf.onSections_add, map_add] } :
      Γ(X, W.1) →+ Γ(X, W.1))
    (fun a b => by
      show e.symm (δ.onSections (e (a * b))) = a * e.symm (δ.onSections (e b)) +
        b * e.symm (δ.onSections (e a))
      rw [map_mul, Stacks.Curves.SheafDerivationOf.onSections_mul, map_add, map_mul, map_mul,
        e.symm_apply_apply, e.symm_apply_apply])
    (fun c => by
      show e.symm (δ.onSections (e (algebraMap k Γ(X, W.1) c))) = 0
      have hb := Stacks.Curves.SheafDerivationOf.onSections_restrict δ
        (U := (V.ι ≫ sX) ⁻¹ᵁ ⊤) (V := V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ W.1) le_top
        (((V.ι ≫ sX).app ⊤).hom ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv.hom c))
      rw [Stacks.Curves.SheafDerivationOf.onSections_app] at hb
      rw [he, iota_app_algebraMap sX V W.1 c]
      erw [hb]
      rw [map_zero, map_zero]), ?_⟩
  intro f
  have key2 : ∀ x, V.topIso.inv.hom (V.topIso.hom.hom x) = x := fun x => by
    rw [← CommRingCat.comp_apply, Iso.hom_inv_id]; rfl
  show _ = e.symm (δ.onSections (e _))
  apply e.injective
  rw [e.apply_symm_apply, he, he, iota_app_restrict hW, iota_app_restrict hW]
  unfold applyDerivation
  rw [key2]
  exact (Stacks.Curves.SheafDerivationOf.onSections_restrict δ (U := ⊤) (V := V.ι ⁻¹ᵁ W.1)
    le_top _).symm

/-- `D(I)` is the ideal sheaf generated by all `δ(f)` with `V ⊆ X` open, `δ ∈ Der_X(V)` a
`k`-derivation of the sheaf `𝒪_V` and `f ∈ I(V)` (Kollár Def. 3.73, (3.73.1)), on a scheme
locally of finite type over `k`. -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_derivative_ideal"]
theorem derivativeIdeal_eq_sInf_sheafDerivation [LocallyOfFiniteType sX] (I : X.IdealSheafData) :
    derivativeIdeal sX I = sInf {J | ∀ (V : X.Opens)
      (δ : Stacks.Curves.SheafDerivationOf (V.ι ≫ sX)) (f : Γ(X, V)),
      IsSectionOf I f → IsSectionOf J (applyDerivation sX δ f)} := by
  unfold derivativeIdeal
  congr 1
  ext J
  simp only [Set.mem_setOf_eq]
  constructor
  · intro hJ V δ f hf W hW
    obtain ⟨δW, hδW⟩ := exists_derivation_of_sheafDerivation sX δ W hW
    rw [hδW f]
    exact hJ W (Ideal.subset_span ⟨δW, _, hf W hW, rfl⟩)
  · intro hJ W
    unfold sectionDerivativeIdeal derivativeIdealOfRing
    refine Ideal.span_le.mpr ?_
    rintro _ ⟨δ, f, hf, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨δ', hδ'⟩ := exists_sheafDerivation_of_derivation sX W δ
    have h := hJ W.1 δ' f (fun W' h' => I.ideal_le_comap_ideal h' hf) W le_rfl
    rw [hδ' f] at h
    simpa using h

/-- The *higher derivatives* `D^r(I)`: `D^0(I) = I` and `D^{r+1}(I) = D(D^r(I))` (Kollár
(3.73.2)). -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_higher_derivative_ideal"]
def higherDerivativeIdeal (I : X.IdealSheafData) (r : ℕ) : X.IdealSheafData :=
  (derivativeIdeal sX)^[r] I

/-- `D^0(I) = I`. -/
@[simp, mmp "def_kr3d_higher_derivative_ideal"]
theorem higherDerivativeIdeal_zero (I : X.IdealSheafData) :
    higherDerivativeIdeal sX I 0 = I := rfl

/-- `D^{r+1}(I) = D(D^r(I))`. -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_higher_derivative_ideal"]
theorem higherDerivativeIdeal_succ (I : X.IdealSheafData) (r : ℕ) :
    higherDerivativeIdeal sX I (r + 1) = derivativeIdeal sX (higherDerivativeIdeal sX I r) :=
  Function.iterate_succ_apply' _ _ _

/-- `D^1(I) = D(I)`. -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_higher_derivative_ideal"]
theorem higherDerivativeIdeal_one (I : X.IdealSheafData) :
    higherDerivativeIdeal sX I 1 = derivativeIdeal sX I := rfl

/-- The *maximal contact ideal* `MC(I) = D^{m-1}(I)`, `m = maxord I` (Kollár Def. 3.79). -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_maximal_contact_ideal"]
def maximalContactIdeal (I : X.IdealSheafData) : X.IdealSheafData :=
  higherDerivativeIdeal sX I ((maxOrder I).toNat - 1)

/-- `I` is *`D`-balanced* (Kollár Def. 3.83 = 3.52): `(D^i(I))^m ⊆ I^{m-i}` for every
`0 ≤ i < m`, `m = maxord I`. -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_d_balanced"]
def IsDBalanced (I : X.IdealSheafData) : Prop :=
  ∀ i < (maxOrder I).toNat,
    higherDerivativeIdeal sX I i ^ (maxOrder I).toNat ≤ I ^ ((maxOrder I).toNat - i)

/-- `I` is *maximal contact invariant* (Kollár 3.53, (3.53.1)–(3.53.2)):
`MC(I)·D(I) ⊆ I`. -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_mc_invariant"]
def IsMCInvariant (I : X.IdealSheafData) : Prop :=
  maximalContactIdeal sX I * derivativeIdeal sX I ≤ I

/-- `I` is maximal contact invariant if and only if `D^{m-1}(I)·D(I) ⊆ I`, `m = maxord I`. -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_mc_invariant"]
theorem isMCInvariant_iff (I : X.IdealSheafData) :
    IsMCInvariant sX I ↔
      higherDerivativeIdeal sX I ((maxOrder I).toNat - 1) * derivativeIdeal sX I ≤ I :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- The *derivative* `D^r(I, m) = (D^r(I), m - r)` of a marked ideal, `0 ≤ r ≤ m` (Kollár
(3.73.3)). -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_marked_derivative"]
def MarkedIdeal.derivative (a : MarkedIdeal X) (r : ℕ) : MarkedIdeal X :=
  ⟨higherDerivativeIdeal sX a.I r, a.m - r⟩

/-- The ideal of `D^r(I, m)` is `D^r(I)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem MarkedIdeal.derivative_I (a : MarkedIdeal X) (r : ℕ) :
    (a.derivative sX r).I = higherDerivativeIdeal sX a.I r := rfl

/-- The order of `D^r(I, m)` is `m - r`. -/
@[simp]
theorem MarkedIdeal.derivative_m (a : MarkedIdeal X) (r : ℕ) :
    (a.derivative sX r).m = a.m - r := rfl

end Sheaf

/-! ### Local coordinates and partial derivatives -/

section Coordinates

variable {k : Type u} [Field k] {X : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ Spec (.of k))

/-- The restriction `Γ(X, U) → Γ(X, W)` to an affine open `W ⊆ U`. -/
def restrictSection {U : X.Opens} (W : X.affineOpens) (h : W.1 ≤ U) (f : Γ(X, U)) :
    Γ(X, W) :=
  (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op).hom f

/-- Sections `x_1, …, x_n ∈ 𝒪_X(U)` are *local coordinates on* the open `U` of a scheme over `k`
(Kollár Def. 3.73): `dx_1, …, dx_n` form a basis of the `𝒪_U`-module `Ω_{U/k}`, i.e. on every
affine open `W ⊆ U` the differentials `d(x_i|_W)` form a basis of `Ω_{𝒪_X(W)/k}`. -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_local_coordinates"]
def IsLocalCoordinatesOn (U : X.Opens) {n : ℕ} (x : Fin n → Γ(X, U)) : Prop :=
  ∀ (W : X.affineOpens) (h : W.1 ≤ U),
    letI := MMP.Mori.sectionAlgebra sX W.1
    ∃ b : Module.Basis (Fin n) Γ(X, W) (KaehlerDifferential k Γ(X, W)),
      ∀ i, b i = KaehlerDifferential.D k Γ(X, W) (restrictSection W h (x i))

/-- Local coordinates `x_1, …, x_n` on `U` are *local coordinates at* `p ∈ U` (Kollár Def. 3.73)
if moreover every `x_i` vanishes at `p`, i.e. its germ lies in `𝔪_p`. -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_local_coordinates"]
def IsLocalCoordinatesAt (U : X.Opens) {n : ℕ} (x : Fin n → Γ(X, U)) (p : X) (hp : p ∈ U) :
    Prop :=
  IsLocalCoordinatesOn sX U x ∧
    ∀ i, (X.presheaf.germ U p hp).hom (x i) ∈ maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk p)

variable {sX} {U : X.Opens} {n : ℕ} {x : Fin n → Γ(X, U)}

/-- The basis `(d(x_i|_W))_i` of `Ω_{𝒪_X(W)/k}` on an affine open `W ⊆ U`. -/
def IsLocalCoordinatesOn.basis (hx : IsLocalCoordinatesOn sX U x) (W : X.affineOpens)
    (h : W.1 ≤ U) :
    letI := MMP.Mori.sectionAlgebra sX W.1
    Module.Basis (Fin n) Γ(X, W) (KaehlerDifferential k Γ(X, W)) :=
  (hx W h).choose

/-- The *partial derivative* `∂g/∂x_i` of a section `g ∈ 𝒪_X(W)` over an affine open `W ⊆ U`
(Kollár Def. 3.73): the coefficient of `dx_i` in the expansion `dg = ∑_i (∂g/∂x_i) dx_i` of
`dg ∈ Ω_{𝒪_X(W)/k}` in the basis `dx_1, …, dx_n`. -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_partial_derivatives"]
def partialDerivative (hx : IsLocalCoordinatesOn sX U x) (W : X.affineOpens) (h : W.1 ≤ U)
    (i : Fin n) (g : Γ(X, W)) : Γ(X, W) :=
  letI := MMP.Mori.sectionAlgebra sX W.1
  (hx.basis W h).repr (KaehlerDifferential.D k Γ(X, W) g) i

/-- `dg = ∑_i (∂g/∂x_i) dx_i` on an affine open `W ⊆ U`. -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_partial_derivatives"]
theorem sum_partialDerivative_smul (hx : IsLocalCoordinatesOn sX U x) (W : X.affineOpens)
    (h : W.1 ≤ U) (g : Γ(X, W)) :
    letI := MMP.Mori.sectionAlgebra sX W.1
    ∑ i, partialDerivative hx W h i g •
        KaehlerDifferential.D k Γ(X, W) (restrictSection W h (x i)) =
      KaehlerDifferential.D k Γ(X, W) g := by
  let := MMP.Mori.sectionAlgebra sX W.1
  have hb : ∀ i, hx.basis W h i = KaehlerDifferential.D k Γ(X, W) (restrictSection W h (x i)) :=
    (hx W h).choose_spec
  simp_rw [← hb]
  exact (hx.basis W h).sum_repr _

private theorem basis_repr_map_aux {A B ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [Algebra k A] [Algebra k B] (φ : A →ₐ[k] B)
    (bA : Module.Basis ι A (KaehlerDifferential k A))
    (bB : Module.Basis ι B (KaehlerDifferential k B)) (a : ι → A)
    (hA : ∀ i, bA i = KaehlerDifferential.D k A (a i))
    (hB : ∀ i, bB i = KaehlerDifferential.D k B (φ (a i))) (g : A) (i : ι) :
    φ (bA.repr (KaehlerDifferential.D k A g) i) =
      bB.repr (KaehlerDifferential.D k B (φ g)) i := by
  let := φ.toRingHom.toAlgebra
  have : IsScalarTower k A B :=
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq' (by ext; simp [RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra])
  have h1 : KaehlerDifferential.map k k A B (KaehlerDifferential.D k A g) =
      KaehlerDifferential.D k B (φ g) := by
    rw [KaehlerDifferential.map_D]; rfl
  have h2 : KaehlerDifferential.map k k A B (KaehlerDifferential.D k A g) =
      ∑ j, φ (bA.repr (KaehlerDifferential.D k A g) j) • bB j := by
    conv_lhs => rw [← bA.sum_repr (KaehlerDifferential.D k A g)]
    rw [map_sum]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => ?_
    rw [map_smul, hA, KaehlerDifferential.map_D, hB]
    rfl
  rw [← h1, h2, Module.Basis.repr_sum_self]

private theorem restrict_restrictSection {W' W : X.affineOpens} (hW : W.1 ≤ U)
    (h' : W'.1 ≤ W.1) (g : Γ(X, U)) :
    (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE h').op).hom (restrictSection W hW g) =
      restrictSection W' (h'.trans hW) g := by
  unfold restrictSection
  rw [← CommRingCat.comp_apply, ← Functor.map_comp]
  rfl

private theorem partialDerivative_restrict
    (hx : IsLocalCoordinatesOn sX U x) (W W' : X.affineOpens) (h : W.1 ≤ U)
    (h' : W'.1 ≤ W.1) (i : Fin n) (g : Γ(X, W)) :
    (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE h').op).hom (partialDerivative hx W h i g) =
      partialDerivative hx W' (h'.trans h) i ((X.presheaf.map (homOfLE h').op).hom g) := by
  let := MMP.Mori.sectionAlgebra sX W.1
  let := MMP.Mori.sectionAlgebra sX W'.1
  let φ : Γ(X, W) →ₐ[k] Γ(X, W') :=
    { (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE h').op).hom with
      commutes' := fun c => sectionAlgebra_res (sX := sX) h' c }
  exact basis_repr_map_aux φ (hx.basis W h) (hx.basis W' (h'.trans h))
    (fun i => restrictSection W h (x i))
    (fun i => (hx W h).choose_spec i)
    (fun i => ((hx W' (h'.trans h)).choose_spec i).trans
      (congrArg _ (restrict_restrictSection h h' (x i)).symm)) g i

private theorem exists_affine_le (V : X.Opens) (p : X) (hp : p ∈ V) :
    ∃ W : X.affineOpens, p ∈ W.1 ∧ W.1 ≤ V := by
  obtain ⟨W, hW, hpW, hWV⟩ := exists_isAffineOpen_mem_and_subset hp
  exact ⟨⟨W, hW⟩, hpW, hWV⟩

/-- For a local section `h ∈ 𝒪_X(U)`, the partial derivatives `∂(h|_W)/∂x_i` over the affine
opens `W ⊆ U` glue to a unique section `∂h/∂x_i ∈ 𝒪_X(U)`. -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_partial_derivatives"]
theorem existsUnique_partialDerivative_glue (hx : IsLocalCoordinatesOn sX U x) (i : Fin n)
    (g : Γ(X, U)) :
    ∃! d : Γ(X, U), ∀ (W : X.affineOpens) (h : W.1 ≤ U),
      restrictSection W h d = partialDerivative hx W h i (restrictSection W h g) := by
  set c : ∀ W : {W : X.affineOpens // W.1 ≤ U}, Γ(X, W.1.1) := fun W =>
    partialDerivative hx W.1 W.2 i (restrictSection W.1 W.2 g) with hc
  have hcres : ∀ (W W' : {W : X.affineOpens // W.1 ≤ U}) (h' : W'.1.1 ≤ W.1.1),
      (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE h').op).hom (c W) = c W' := by
    intro W W' h'
    simp only [hc]
    rw [partialDerivative_restrict hx W.1 W'.1 W.2 h', restrict_restrictSection W.2 h' g]
  have hext : ∀ {V : X.Opens} (s t : Γ(X, V)),
      (∀ (W : X.affineOpens) (hW : W.1 ≤ V),
        (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hW).op).hom s = (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hW).op).hom t) →
      s = t := by
    intro V s t hst
    refine TopCat.Presheaf.IsSheaf.section_ext X.sheaf.property ?_
    intro p hp
    obtain ⟨W, hpW, hWV⟩ := exists_affine_le V p hp
    exact ⟨W.1, hWV, hpW, hst W hWV⟩
  have hcover : U ≤ ⨆ W : {W : X.affineOpens // W.1 ≤ U}, W.1.1 := by
    intro p hp
    obtain ⟨W, hpW, hWU⟩ := exists_affine_le U p hp
    exact Opens.mem_iSup.mpr ⟨⟨W, hWU⟩, hpW⟩
  have hcompat : TopCat.Presheaf.IsCompatible X.presheaf (fun W : {W : X.affineOpens // W.1 ≤ U} =>
      W.1.1) c := by
    intro W W'
    refine TopCat.Presheaf.IsSheaf.section_ext X.sheaf.property ?_
    intro p hp
    obtain ⟨V, hpV, hVle⟩ := exists_affine_le (W.1.1 ⊓ W'.1.1) p hp
    refine ⟨V.1, hVle, hpV, ?_⟩
    have e1 := hcres W ⟨V, (hVle.trans inf_le_left).trans W.2⟩ (hVle.trans inf_le_left)
    have e2 := hcres W' ⟨V, (hVle.trans inf_le_left).trans W.2⟩ (hVle.trans inf_le_right)
    show (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVle).op).hom ((X.presheaf.map (Opens.infLELeft _ _).op).hom
        (c W)) = (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVle).op).hom
        ((X.presheaf.map (Opens.infLERight _ _).op).hom (c W'))
    rw [← CommRingCat.comp_apply, ← CommRingCat.comp_apply, ← Functor.map_comp,
      ← Functor.map_comp]
    exact e1.trans e2.symm
  obtain ⟨d, hd, -⟩ := X.sheaf.existsUnique_gluing' (fun W : {W : X.affineOpens // W.1 ≤ U} =>
    W.1.1) U (fun W => homOfLE W.2) hcover c hcompat
  have hd' : ∀ (W : X.affineOpens) (h : W.1 ≤ U),
      restrictSection W h d = partialDerivative hx W h i (restrictSection W h g) :=
    fun W h => hd ⟨W, h⟩
  refine ⟨d, hd', fun d' hd'' => hext _ _ fun W hW => ?_⟩
  exact (hd'' W hW).trans (hd' W hW).symm

variable (sX) in
/-- The ideals `∂^r_{x_i} J` of an ideal sheaf `J` on a scheme `Y` over `k` with local
coordinates `x_1, …, x_n` on `Y` (Kollár (3.87.2), stated for `Y = U`):
`∂^0_{x_i} J = J` and `∂^{r+1}_{x_i} J` is the ideal sheaf generated by the `∂f/∂x_i`, `f` a local
section of `∂^r_{x_i} J`. -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_partial_derivative_ideal"]
def partialDerivativeIdeal {x : Fin n → Γ(X, ⊤)} (hx : IsLocalCoordinatesOn sX ⊤ x) (i : Fin n)
    (J : X.IdealSheafData) (r : ℕ) : X.IdealSheafData :=
  (fun J' : X.IdealSheafData => sInf {J'' : X.IdealSheafData | ∀ (W : X.affineOpens),
      ∀ f ∈ J'.ideal W, partialDerivative hx W le_top i f ∈ J''.ideal W})^[r] J

variable (sX) in
/-- `∂^0_{x_i} J = J`. -/
@[simp]
theorem partialDerivativeIdeal_zero {x : Fin n → Γ(X, ⊤)} (hx : IsLocalCoordinatesOn sX ⊤ x)
    (i : Fin n) (J : X.IdealSheafData) : partialDerivativeIdeal sX hx i J 0 = J := rfl

variable (sX) in
/-- `∂^{r+1}_{x_i} J` is generated by the `∂f/∂x_i`, `f` a local section of `∂^r_{x_i} J`. -/
theorem partialDerivativeIdeal_succ {x : Fin n → Γ(X, ⊤)} (hx : IsLocalCoordinatesOn sX ⊤ x)
    (i : Fin n) (J : X.IdealSheafData) (r : ℕ) :
    partialDerivativeIdeal sX hx i J (r + 1) = sInf {J'' : X.IdealSheafData |
      ∀ (W : X.affineOpens), ∀ f ∈ (partialDerivativeIdeal sX hx i J r).ideal W,
        partialDerivative hx W le_top i f ∈ J''.ideal W} :=
  Function.iterate_succ_apply' _ _ _

end Coordinates

/-! ### Logarithmic derivations -/

section Log

variable {k : Type u} [Field k] {X : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ Spec (.of k))

/-- The *logarithmic derivations* `Der_X(-log S)(W)` along a hypersurface `S ⊆ X` over an affine
open `W` (Kollár 3.87): the `k`-derivations `δ` of `𝒪_X(W)` with `δ(𝒪_X(-S)(W)) ⊆ 𝒪_X(-S)(W)`. -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_log_derivations"]
def logDerivations (S : X.IdealSheafData) (W : X.affineOpens) :
    letI := MMP.Mori.sectionAlgebra sX W.1
    Submodule Γ(X, W) (Derivation k Γ(X, W) Γ(X, W)) :=
  letI := MMP.Mori.sectionAlgebra sX W.1
  { carrier := {δ | ∀ f ∈ S.ideal W, δ f ∈ S.ideal W}
    add_mem' := fun ha hb f hf => by
      simpa using Ideal.add_mem _ (ha f hf) (hb f hf)
    zero_mem' := fun f _ => by simp
    smul_mem' := fun c δ hδ f hf => by
      simpa using Ideal.mul_mem_left _ c (hδ f hf) }

/-- `δ` is a logarithmic derivation along `S` iff it maps `𝒪_X(-S)(W)` into itself. -/
@[simp]
theorem mem_logDerivations_iff (S : X.IdealSheafData) (W : X.affineOpens)
    (δ : letI := MMP.Mori.sectionAlgebra sX W.1; Derivation k Γ(X, W) Γ(X, W)) :
    δ ∈ logDerivations sX S W ↔ ∀ f ∈ S.ideal W, δ f ∈ S.ideal W := Iff.rfl

/-- The ideal of `Γ(X, W)` generated by the `δ(f)`, `δ ∈ Der_X(-log S)(W)` and `f ∈ I(W)`. -/
def sectionLogDerivativeIdeal (S I : X.IdealSheafData) (W : X.affineOpens) : Ideal Γ(X, W) :=
  letI := MMP.Mori.sectionAlgebra sX W.1
  Ideal.span {g | ∃ δ ∈ logDerivations sX S W, ∃ f ∈ I.ideal W, δ f = g}

/-- The *logarithmic derivative* `D(-log S)(I)` of an ideal sheaf (Kollár 3.87): the ideal sheaf
generated by all `δ(f)`, `δ` a local section of `Der_X(-log S)` and `f` a local section of `I`. -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_log_derivative_ideal"]
def logDerivativeIdeal (S I : X.IdealSheafData) : X.IdealSheafData :=
  sInf {J | ∀ W : X.affineOpens, sectionLogDerivativeIdeal sX S I W ≤ J.ideal W}

/-- The *higher logarithmic derivatives* `D^r(-log S)(I)`: `D^0(-log S)(I) = I` and
`D^{r+1}(-log S)(I) = D(-log S)(D^r(-log S)(I))` (Kollár 3.87). -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_log_derivative_ideal"]
def higherLogDerivativeIdeal (S I : X.IdealSheafData) (r : ℕ) : X.IdealSheafData :=
  (logDerivativeIdeal sX S)^[r] I

/-- `D^0(-log S)(I) = I`. -/
@[simp]
theorem higherLogDerivativeIdeal_zero (S I : X.IdealSheafData) :
    higherLogDerivativeIdeal sX S I 0 = I := rfl

/-- `D^{r+1}(-log S)(I) = D(-log S)(D^r(-log S)(I))`. -/
theorem higherLogDerivativeIdeal_succ (S I : X.IdealSheafData) (r : ℕ) :
    higherLogDerivativeIdeal sX S I (r + 1) =
      logDerivativeIdeal sX S (higherLogDerivativeIdeal sX S I r) :=
  Function.iterate_succ_apply' _ _ _

/-- For `S = ∅` (ideal `⊤`) the logarithmic derivatives are the derivatives `D^r(I)`. -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_log_derivative_ideal"]
theorem higherLogDerivativeIdeal_top (I : X.IdealSheafData) (r : ℕ) :
    higherLogDerivativeIdeal sX ⊤ I r = higherDerivativeIdeal sX I r := by
  have : logDerivativeIdeal sX ⊤ = derivativeIdeal sX := by
    funext J
    have hW : ∀ W, sectionLogDerivativeIdeal sX ⊤ J W = sectionDerivativeIdeal sX J W := by
      intro W
      let := MMP.Mori.sectionAlgebra sX W.1
      unfold sectionLogDerivativeIdeal sectionDerivativeIdeal derivativeIdealOfRing
      congr 1
      ext g
      simp only [Set.mem_ofPred_eq]
      exact ⟨fun ⟨δ, _, f, hf, hg⟩ => ⟨δ, f, hf, hg⟩,
        fun ⟨δ, f, hf, hg⟩ => ⟨δ, fun _ _ => by simp, f, hf, hg⟩⟩
    simp only [logDerivativeIdeal, derivativeIdeal, hW]
  simp only [higherLogDerivativeIdeal, higherDerivativeIdeal, this]

/-- The *logarithmic derivative* `D^j(-log S)(I, m) = (D^j(-log S)(I), m - j)` of a marked ideal,
`0 ≤ j ≤ m` (Kollár (3.87.3), (3.88.1)). -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_marked_log_derivative"]
def MarkedIdeal.logDerivative (S : X.IdealSheafData) (a : MarkedIdeal X) (j : ℕ) :
    MarkedIdeal X :=
  ⟨higherLogDerivativeIdeal sX S a.I j, a.m - j⟩

/-- The ideal of `D^j(-log S)(I, m)` is `D^j(-log S)(I)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem MarkedIdeal.logDerivative_I (S : X.IdealSheafData) (a : MarkedIdeal X) (j : ℕ) :
    (a.logDerivative sX S j).I = higherLogDerivativeIdeal sX S a.I j := rfl

/-- The order of `D^j(-log S)(I, m)` is `m - j`. -/
@[simp]
theorem MarkedIdeal.logDerivative_m (S : X.IdealSheafData) (a : MarkedIdeal X) (j : ℕ) :
    (a.logDerivative sX S j).m = a.m - j := rfl

end Log

/-! ### The transforms `T_i(K, a)` of Cor. 3.77 -/

namespace ClosedBlowupSequence

/-- One step `T ↦ 𝒪(aF)·π^*T` (if `T ⊆ 𝒪_X`, `0` otherwise) of the recursion of Cor. 3.77 along
the blow-up of `Z`, `F = π⁻¹(Z)`; `none` stands for a fractional ideal sheaf not contained in
`𝒪`. -/
def derivedTransformStep {X : Scheme.{u}} (Z : X.IdealSheafData) (a : ℕ) :
    Option X.IdealSheafData → Option (blowUp Z).IdealSheafData
  | none => some ⊥
  | some J =>
    open Classical in
    if J.comap (blowUpToBase Z) ≤ Z.comap (blowUpToBase Z) ^ a then
      some (idealColon (J.comap (blowUpToBase Z)) (Z.comap (blowUpToBase Z) ^ a))
    else none

/-- The transform `T_r(K, a)` on `X_r` along a blow-up sequence `(X_i, Z_i)_{i ≤ r}` (Kollár
Cor. 3.77): `T_0(K, a) = K` and `T_{i+1}(K, a) = 𝒪_{X_{i+1}}(aF_{i+1})·π_i^*T_i(K, a)` if
`T_i(K, a) ⊆ 𝒪_{X_i}`, `T_{i+1}(K, a) = 0` otherwise, `F_{i+1} = π_i⁻¹(Z_i)`. The value is
`some J` when `T_r(K, a) = J` is an ideal sheaf and `none` when `T_r(K, a)` is a fractional ideal
sheaf not contained in `𝒪_{X_r}`. The earlier `T_i` are those of `B.truncate i`. -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_derived_transform_sequence"]
def derivedTransform : {X : Scheme.{u}} → (B : ClosedBlowupSequence X) →
    Option X.IdealSheafData → ℕ → Option B.target.IdealSheafData
  | _, nil _, T, _ => T
  | _, cons Z B, T, a => B.derivedTransform (derivedTransformStep Z a T) a

/-- If `T_i(K, a) ⊆ 𝒪_{X_i}`, then `T_{i+1}(K, a)` is `𝒪(aF)·π^*T_i(K, a)`: whenever it is an
ideal sheaf, multiplied by `𝒪(-aF) = I_F^a` it gives back `π^*T_i(K, a)`. -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_derived_transform_sequence"]
theorem derivedTransformStep_mul_eq {X : Scheme.{u}} (Z : X.IdealSheafData) (a : ℕ)
    (J : X.IdealSheafData) (J' : (blowUp Z).IdealSheafData)
    (h : derivedTransformStep Z a (some J) = some J')
    (hZ : Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor (Z.comap (blowUpToBase Z))) :
    J' * Z.comap (blowUpToBase Z) ^ a = J.comap (blowUpToBase Z) := by
  classical
  have hZa : Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor (Z.comap (blowUpToBase Z) ^ a) :=
    Stacks.Divisors.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_pow hZ a
  simp only [derivedTransformStep] at h
  split_ifs at h with hle
  · cases h
    have hcol : idealColon (J.comap (blowUpToBase Z)) (Z.comap (blowUpToBase Z) ^ a) =
        Scheme.IdealSheafData.colon (J.comap (blowUpToBase Z)) (Z.comap (blowUpToBase Z) ^ a)
          (AlgebraicGeometry.fg_ideal_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor _ hZa) := by
      unfold idealColon
      exact Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdeals_ideal
        (Scheme.IdealSheafData.colon (J.comap (blowUpToBase Z)) (Z.comap (blowUpToBase Z) ^ a)
          (AlgebraicGeometry.fg_ideal_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor _ hZa))
    rw [hcol, mul_comm]
    exact AlgebraicGeometry.mul_colon_eq_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor _ _ hZa hle

variable {k : Type u} [Field k]

/-- Kollár's `J_r = T_r(D^j(I), m - j)` of Cor. 3.77 for a marked ideal `(I, m)` and
`0 ≤ j ≤ m`. -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_derived_transform_sequence"]
def derivedTransformJ {X : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)) (B : ClosedBlowupSequence X)
    (a : MarkedIdeal X) (j : ℕ) : Option B.target.IdealSheafData :=
  B.derivedTransform (some (higherDerivativeIdeal sX a.I j)) (a.m - j)

/-! ### Hypersurfaces of maximal contact -/

/-- Along the restriction `(S_i)` of a blow-up sequence `(X_i, Z_i)` to `S` (pull-back along
`j : S → X`, with `j_{i+1}` the canonical lift of `j_i`), every center `Z_i` is contained in the
closed subscheme `S_i` of `X_i` (the scheme-theoretic image of `j_i`): `I_{S_i} ⊆ I_{Z_i}`. -/
def CentersContainedIn : {X S : Scheme.{u}} → ClosedBlowupSequence X → (S ⟶ X) → Prop
  | _, _, nil _, _ => True
  | _, _, cons Z B, j => j.ker ≤ Z ∧ B.CentersContainedIn (canonicalLift j Z)

end ClosedBlowupSequence

section MaximalContact

variable {k : Type u} [Field k] {X : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ Spec (.of k))

/-- A closed subscheme `H ⊆ X` is a *hypersurface of maximal contact* for `I` (Kollár
Def. 3.78): `H` is a smooth hypersurface (smooth over `k`, of pure codimension one, possibly
empty), and for every open `X⁰ ⊆ X` and every smooth blow-up sequence `(X⁰_i, Z_i)` of order
`m = maxord I` starting with `(X⁰, I|_{X⁰})`, with `(H⁰_i)` its restriction to `H⁰ = H ∩ X⁰`,
every center `Z_i` is contained in `H⁰_i`. -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_hypersurface_of_maximal_contact"]
def IsHypersurfaceOfMaximalContact (I H : X.IdealSheafData) : Prop :=
  MMP.Mori.IsSmoothScheme (H.subschemeι ≫ sX) ∧ MMP.Mori.IsPureCodimOne H.support ∧
    ∀ (X₀ : X.Opens) (B : ClosedBlowupSequence X₀),
      B.IsOrderMPlainSeq (X₀.ι ≫ sX) (I.comap X₀.ι) (maxOrder I).toNat →
        B.CentersContainedIn (H.comap X₀.ι).subschemeι

/-! ### Étale equivalence -/

/-- A pair of étale morphisms `ψ, ψ' : U → X` of `k`-schemes, `U` of finite type over `k`, whose
images contain `cosupp(I, m)`, `m = maxord I`, with `ψ^*I = ψ'^*I` and
`(ψ, ψ')^*(I_Δ) ⊆ D^{m-1}(ψ^*I)`, `I_Δ` the ideal sheaf of the diagonal of `X ×_k X` (the
common conditions of Kollár Def. 3.96 and §3.10). -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_etale_equivalence_of_blowup_sequences"]
structure IsEtaleChartPair (I : X.IdealSheafData) {U : Scheme.{u}} (sU : U ⟶ Spec (.of k))
    (ψ ψ' : U ⟶ X) : Prop where
  /-- `U` is locally of finite type over `k`. -/
  locallyOfFiniteType : LocallyOfFiniteType sU
  /-- `U` is quasi-compact over `k`. -/
  quasiCompact : QuasiCompact sU
  /-- `ψ` is étale. -/
  etale : Etale ψ
  /-- `ψ'` is étale. -/
  etale' : Etale ψ'
  /-- `ψ` is a morphism of `k`-schemes. -/
  comp_eq : ψ ≫ sX = sU
  /-- `ψ'` is a morphism of `k`-schemes. -/
  comp_eq' : ψ' ≫ sX = sU
  /-- The image of `ψ` contains `cosupp(I, m)`. -/
  cosupport_subset : (⟨I, (maxOrder I).toNat⟩ : MarkedIdeal X).cosupport ⊆ Set.range ψ
  /-- The image of `ψ'` contains `cosupp(I, m)`. -/
  cosupport_subset' : (⟨I, (maxOrder I).toNat⟩ : MarkedIdeal X).cosupport ⊆ Set.range ψ'
  /-- `ψ^*I = ψ'^*I`. -/
  comap_eq : I.comap ψ = I.comap ψ'
  /-- `(ψ, ψ')^*(I_Δ) ⊆ D^{m-1}(ψ^*I)`. -/
  diagonal_le : (pullback.diagonal sX).ker.comap (pullback.lift ψ ψ' (comp_eq.trans comp_eq'.symm))
    ≤ higherDerivativeIdeal sU (I.comap ψ) ((maxOrder I).toNat - 1)

/-- Two blow-up sequences `𝐁, 𝐁'` starting with `X` are *étale equivalent* with respect to `I`
(Kollár Def. 3.96): there are a scheme `U` of finite type over `k` and étale morphisms
`ψ, ψ' : U → X` whose images contain `cosupp(I, m)` with (1) `ψ^*I = ψ'^*I`,
(2) `(ψ, ψ')^*(I_Δ) ⊆ D^{m-1}(ψ^*I)` and (3) `ψ^*𝐁 = ψ'^*𝐁'` (same length and same centers). -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_etale_equivalence_of_blowup_sequences"]
def ClosedBlowupSequence.AreEtaleEquivalent (I : X.IdealSheafData)
    (B B' : ClosedBlowupSequence X) : Prop :=
  ∃ (U : Scheme.{u}) (sU : U ⟶ Spec (.of k)) (ψ ψ' : U ⟶ X),
    IsEtaleChartPair sX I sU ψ ψ' ∧ B.pullback ψ = B'.pullback ψ'

/-- Hypersurfaces `H, H' ⊆ X` are *étale equivalent with respect to `(X, I, E)`* (Kollár §3.10):
there are a scheme `U` of finite type over `k` and étale morphisms `ψ, ψ' : U → X` whose images
contain `cosupp(I, m)` with (1′) `ψ⁻¹(H) = ψ'⁻¹(H')`, (2′) `ψ^*I = ψ'^*I`,
(3′) `ψ⁻¹(E^i) = ψ'⁻¹(E^i)` for every `i`, and (4′) `(ψ, ψ')^*(I_Δ) ⊆ D^{m-1}(ψ^*I)`. -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_etale_equivalence_of_hypersurfaces"]
def AreEtaleEquivalentHypersurfaces (I : X.IdealSheafData) (E : OrderedDivisor X)
    (H H' : X.IdealSheafData) : Prop :=
  ∃ (U : Scheme.{u}) (sU : U ⟶ Spec (.of k)) (ψ ψ' : U ⟶ X),
    IsEtaleChartPair sX I sU ψ ψ' ∧ H.comap ψ = H'.comap ψ' ∧
      ∀ i, (E.E i).comap ψ = (E.E i).comap ψ'

/-! ### Formal equivalence -/

/-- The completion `Ĵ = J·𝒪̂_{p,X}` of an ideal sheaf `J` at `p`. -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_formal_equivalence_of_maximal_contact"]
def completedIdeal (J : X.IdealSheafData) (p : X) :
    Ideal (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk p)) (X.presheaf.stalk p)) :=
  (IdealSheafData.stalk J p).map
    (algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk p)
      (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk p)) (X.presheaf.stalk p)))

/-- The `k`-algebra structure of the completed local ring `𝒪̂_{p,X}`. -/
@[instance_reducible]
def completedAlgebra (p : X) :
    Algebra k (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk p)) (X.presheaf.stalk p)) :=
  letI := MMP.Mori.stalkAlgebra sX p
  ((algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk p)
      (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk p)) (X.presheaf.stalk p))).comp
    (algebraMap k (X.presheaf.stalk p))).toAlgebra

/-- Hypersurfaces `H, H' ⊆ X` are *formally equivalent at `p` with respect to `(X, I, E)`*
(Kollár Def. 3.91), `m = maxord I`: there is a `k`-algebra automorphism `φ^*` of `𝒪̂ = 𝒪̂_{p,X}`
with (1) `φ^*(Î_{H'}) = Î_H`, (2) `φ^*(Î) = Î`, (3) `φ^*(Î_{E^i}) = Î_{E^i}` for every `i`, and
(4) `h - φ^*(h) ∈ D^{m-1}(Î)` for every `h ∈ 𝒪̂`, with `D^{m-1} = D^{m-1}_{𝒪̂/k}`. -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_formal_equivalence_of_maximal_contact"]
def AreFormallyEquivalent (p : X) (I : X.IdealSheafData) (E : OrderedDivisor X)
    (H H' : X.IdealSheafData) : Prop :=
  letI := completedAlgebra sX p
  ∃ φ : AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk p)) (X.presheaf.stalk p) ≃ₐ[k]
      AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk p)) (X.presheaf.stalk p),
    (completedIdeal H' p).map φ = completedIdeal H p ∧
      (completedIdeal I p).map φ = completedIdeal I p ∧
      (∀ i, (completedIdeal (E.E i) p).map φ = completedIdeal (E.E i) p) ∧
      ∀ h, h - φ h ∈ higherDerivativeIdealOfRing k (completedIdeal I p) ((maxOrder I).toNat - 1)

end MaximalContact

/-! ### Automorphisms of the form `1 + B` -/

/-- A substitution `g^* : f ↦ f(g_1, …, g_n)` of `R = K[[x_1, …, x_n]]`, `g ∈ 𝔪^n`, is an
*automorphism of the form `1 + B`* for an ideal `B ⊆ 𝔪` (Kollár Notation 3.93): `g^*` is an
automorphism of `R` and `g_i - x_i ∈ B` for every `i`. -/
@[mmp "def_kr3d_automorphism_of_form_one_plus_ideal"]
def IsAutomorphismOfFormOnePlus {K : Type*} [Field K] {n : ℕ}
    (B : Ideal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) K)) (g : Fin n → MvPowerSeries (Fin n) K) : Prop :=
  (∀ i, MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff (g i) = 0) ∧
    Function.Bijective
      (MvPowerSeries.subst (R := K) g : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) K → MvPowerSeries (Fin n) K) ∧
    ∀ i, g i - MvPowerSeries.X i ∈ B

end MMP.Resolution
